# Minecraft craftsmanship (not millimetre OSM)

Full guide: `site/CRAFTSMANSHIP.txt`. OSM/LIDAR/photos set **where** and **what**;
this rule is **how** blocks are placed. Prefer a careful human build.

## Footprint
- On the surveyed plot only (never pavement — I-009).
- Square long runs, clean corners, match party walls; nudge ±1–2 when photo +
  aerial still agree. Do not diamond-trace every OSM jag.

## Fabric
- **Airtight shell** — no holes at corners, eaves, bays, roof joins.
- **Glass:** punch from solids; opaque L/R flanks; sill + lintel/head.
  No floating panes, no glass corners, no glass with air beside it.
- Bays are structural bumps from the ground, not stick-on frames.

## Roofs (pitch is arithmetic)
- Ridge type/direction from aerial; Y from LIDAR. Then pick rise÷run.
- **Victorian/Edwardian terraces (Broadlands Rd type): slate at ~40° →
  45° `deepslate_tile_stairs`, ridge parallel to the street.** Build them with
  `scripts/terrace.py` (see terrace-builds.mdc) — do not hand-roll roofs.
  (The old "default 1:2 slabs" rule read as flat roofs and is withdrawn for
  these; 1:2 slabs only for genuinely shallow modern roofs.)
- Visible roof surface = one sealed skin (stairs at 45°, slabs for shallow). Full blocks are
  wall-plate / gable / hip fill — never a stepped full-block pyramid and
  never Geocraft carpet/stone lattice left as the roof.
- Overhang ≥1 past walls; flat ceiling under the attic; chimney through the
  roof, not parked beside it.

## Processed ground holds no Geocraft
- **Nothing of Geocraft survives on ground a build processes.** Every column
  of every parcel the build covers (house, front garden, back garden, and
  any road/path/gap parcel it takes) is rebuilt or deliberately cleared:
  carpet roofs, stone band / undercroft, stock pavement in gardens, stray
  wall blocks, procedural trees. No "envelope" limit, no later tidy-up pass.
- A Geocraft fragment that straddles the plot line (e.g. carpet fringe just
  outside the OSM cells) is cleared **whole** by the build that owns the
  house it belonged to.
- Also strip stair-skins and other remnants of earlier refine applies on the
  same ground.
- Never leave full brick (or other wall blocks) **above** the roof skin in a column; eaves slab ≥ wall top on the footprint; one chimney stack only.
- Before apply, the preview must show no Geocraft on the plot; after apply,
  `coverage.py signoff` must pass (no override; to keep a Geocraft block
  on purpose, write it in the plan).

## Reject in preview (hard fail — fix before apply)
Lattice/striped carpet roofs, stair-only roofs on shallow pitches, stepped
full-block roof pyramids, flush hats, unflanked glass, jagged OSM
knife-walls, any Geocraft block left on/beside the plot.

## Good enough
Readable sealed massing + street character beats pixel OSM. Still whole
property (all sides, floors + stair, both gardens). No chimney-pot chase.
